      "declare": true,
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": " @target: es2015"
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": " April 2014, Section 4.6:"
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": "      In the absence of a contextual type, the type of an array literal is C[], where C is the"
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": "      Undefined type(section 3.2.6) if the array literal is empty, or the best common type of"
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": "      the element expressions if the array literal is not empty."
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": "      When an array literal is contextually typed(section 4.19) by an object type containing a"
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": "      numeric index signature of type T, each element expression is contextually typed by T and"
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": "      the type of the array literal is the best common type of T and the types of the element"
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": "      expressions."
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": ""
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": " While the spec does not say it, an inferential type causes an empty array literal to have"
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": " the undefined[] type. In other words, the first clause from the excerpt above applies even"
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": " though there is a \"contextual type\" present. This is the intention, even though the spec"
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": " seems to imply the contrary."
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": " Therefore, the following access to bar should not cause an error because we infer"
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": " the undefined[] type."
        }
      ]
    },
